    "case_summary": "A 47-year-old woman self-reported a palpable mass in the outer upper quadrant of the left breast that had been present for more than 2 years, with obvious size increase over the last half year. The patient had no previous medical history, no relevant family history, and no history of previous surgery.\n\nA palpable mass was present in the outer upper quadrant of the left breast.\n\n{'Imaging Studies': {'Ultrasound': {'Finding': 'Regular color Doppler ultrasound revealed irregular hypoechoic areas in the left breast and clear echo boundaries of multiple lymph nodes in the left axilla, with no obvious abnormal blood flow signal in the bilateral breasts.', 'Image Title': 'Preoperative subsidiary exams (first part) - Ultrasound', 'Image Description': 'Irregular hypoechoic areas in left breast with multiple lymph nodes in left axilla'}, 'Mammogram': {'Finding': 'The molybdenum target showed a patchy tortuous structure in the upper outer quadrant of the left mammary gland accompanied by punctate calcification and calcium salt deposition, but no definite mass shadow was found.', 'Image Title': 'Preoperative subsidiary exams (first part) - Mammogram', 'Image Description': 'Patchy tortuous structure with punctate calcification in upper outer quadrant of left breast'}, 'MRI': {'Finding': 'Bilateral breasts were symmetrical, with heterogeneous fibro glandular and multiple nodules. There was an irregular mass in the upper outer quadrant of the left breast with increased number of left axillary lymph nodes.', 'Image Title': 'Preoperative subsidiary exams (second part) - MRI', 'Image Description': 'Irregular mass in upper outer quadrant of left breast with enlarged axillary lymph nodes'}, 'PET-CT': {'Finding': 'Isodense soft tissue mass in the upper outer quadrant of the left breast, with ill-defined boundaries and uniform density. Mass size approximately 4.1 cm x 2.7 cm x 2.9 cm with abnormal radioactive distribution. Several small lymph nodes in left axillary region, some with mildly concentrated radioactivity. No bone, lung, liver, or brain metastasis.', 'Image Title': 'Preoperative subsidiary exams (second part) - PET-CT', 'Image Description': 'Isodense mass with abnormal radioactive uptake in left breast'}}, 'Pathological Tests': {'FNAC Results': 'Microscopically, tumor cells presented variety of arrangement patterns including vesicular, tubular, and striated patterns. No vascular or nerve invasion seen.', 'Immunohistochemistry': 'AR (moderate strength positive), E-Cadherin (+), Ki-67 (positive index about 40%), SOX10 (+), S100 (+), GCDFP-15 (+), PASD (+), PD-L1 (combined positive score = 3)'}}",
